{# THE AREAS — one row per area: how much ground it holds, what it runs, and
   what the modules in it report.

   AN AREA THAT RUNS NOTHING KEEPS ITS ROW, and that is the point of the
   card: it contributes to no figure and appears in no queue anywhere else,
   precisely because it has no module to contribute one, so this is the only
   place it can be seen.

   THE OPERATIONAL COLUMNS ARE THE MODULES' OWN, read from the same now-tiles
   the areas register reads — the host writes the name, the ground and the
   module count, and states no figure it does not own. A column exists only
   where a module contributed one, which is why an installation with nothing
   switched on shows three columns and not five full of noughts. #}
<div class="c" data-w="areas">
    <span class="tab">The areas<span class="src">&middot; {{ areaCounts.all }} &middot; {{ areaCounts.live }} live &middot; {{ areaCounts.setup }} awaiting setup</span></span>
    <a class="more" href="{{ path('area_index') }}">The areas register &rarr;</a>
    <span class="ao-by"><i></i>the organization</span>

    {% if areas is empty %}
        <p class="zeb">No area is registered yet. An area is the place every record resolves to, so it is the first thing an installation gets.</p>
    {% else %}
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr>
                <th>area</th>
                <th>modules</th>
                {% for column in statColumns %}<th>{{ column|lower }}</th>{% endfor %}
                <th>state</th>
            </tr>
            {% for row in areas %}
                <tr>
                    <td{{ row.isLive ? '' : ' class="fog"' }}>
                        <b>{{ row.area.name }}</b>
                        {% if row.areaKm2 %}<span class="mono">{{ row.areaKm2|number_format }} km&sup2;</span>{% endif %}
                    </td>
                    <td class="{{ row.liveModules ? 'g' : 'fog' }}">{{ row.liveModules }}</td>
                    {% for at in 0..(statColumns|length - 1) %}
                        {% if statColumns|length %}
                            <td class="{{ row.stats[at] is defined ? '' : 'fog' }}">
                                {{- row.stats[at] is defined ? row.stats[at].value : '—' -}}
                            </td>
                        {% endif %}
                    {% endfor %}
                    <td><span class="chip {{ row.isLive ? 'ok' : 'idle' }}">{{ row.isLive ? 'live' : 'awaiting setup' }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>
    {% endif %}
</div>
